WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.864
Welcome to our intro to Brand Analytics.

00:00:02.864 --> 00:00:09.000
Brands enrolled in Amazon Brand Registry enjoy access to a suite of additional selling benefits.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
One of those benefits is a group of reports called Brand Analytics.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.462
Brand Analytics reports provide aggregate product and customer information along with competitive

00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:21.000
insights.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.200
They can be used to better understand a brand's performance in the Amazon store and to make strategic

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.000
data-driven decisions about products and advertising.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.667
You can access Brand Analytics anytime if you're a seller internal to a brand enrolled in Brand

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:37.000
Registry.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:45.160
Simply select Brands in the main menu in Seller Central, then click Brand Analytics, or click All

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.000
Brand Benefits, then locate the Brand Analytics card.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.111
For more information about accessing Brand Analytics and other Brand Registry tools, see our modules

00:00:55.111 --> 00:01:00.000
in Seller University about requesting or managing access to Brand Selling Benefits.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.579
After accessing the Brand Analytics tool, you'll see a tab for each report across the top of the

00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:08.000
screen.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.300
Let's quickly review the metrics you'll find in each report and how they can help you enhance your

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.000
brand's performance.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.429
You can use the Search Catalog Performance Report to understand how customers interact with your

00:01:21.429 --> 00:01:24.000
products after searching the Amazon store.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.818
The report lists your brand's products and pairs them with a sequence of metrics that represents

00:01:29.818 --> 00:01:32.000
customer activity throughout the shopping funnel.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Those metrics include impressions, clicks, cart adds, and purchases.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Along with other information in the report, these metrics can help you understand customer drop-

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.000
off points for your products,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.000
and they can help you identify gaps in discoverability or sales conversion.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:56.300
You can use the Search Query Performance Report to see how customers search for your brand in the

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.000
Amazon store.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.000
The report lists top customer queries associated with your brand's products.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:09.111
It pairs them with a sequence of metrics that includes query volume, impressions, clicks, cart adds,

00:02:09.111 --> 00:02:10.000
and purchases.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:16.000
Similar information can also be displayed for a single product using an ASIN view.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.000
Both views can help you understand how customers discover your products,

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.000
or they can help you identify trends and opportunities to expand your product catalog.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.737
You can use the Repeat Purchase Behavior Report to understand how often customers buy your products

00:02:32.737 --> 00:02:34.000
more than once.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.000
The report lists each of your brands according to the total number of orders received.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.000
It pairs them with the amount in sales associated with repeat purchases,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.000
along with the number of units ordered and the number of repeat customers.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.000
You can find similar information at the product level using the ASIN view.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Both views can help you better understand your brand's customer engagement,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.000
and they can help you assess satisfaction with your products.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:08.000
You can use the Demographics Report to get a breakdown of your brand's sales by customer age,

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.000
income, education, gender, and marital status.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.000
The report divides each of these categories into segments,

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.000
then lists the number of unique customers and the number of units ordered.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:27.000
This and other information in the report can help you better understand who's buying your products,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.000
and it can help you define advertising strategies.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.000
The top search terms report provides brands with a broad view of customer search activity.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:41.000
Instead of focusing exclusively on your brand, like the Search Catalog Performance

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:47.176
and Search Query Performance Reports, the top search terms report lists keywords that customers

00:03:47.176 --> 00:03:48.000
have used

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.000
to find and purchase products across the Amazon store.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:59.500
It pairs each keyword with the three most clicked products, categories, and brands from customer

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.000
searches.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.545
This and other information in the report can help you suggest updates to the keywords associated

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:09.000
with your brand's product detail pages,

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:14.000
or it can help you identify purchasing trends and advertising opportunities.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.647
Finally, you can use the Market Basket Analysis Report to see other products that customers are

00:04:19.647 --> 00:04:20.000
buying

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:24.000
when they purchase products that are part of your brand.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.000
The report lists your brand's products and pairs them with the three products

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:35.000
that are most frequently purchased at the same time, whether they belong to your brand or a competitor.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:41.588
This and other information in the report can help you identify opportunities to bundle your brand's

00:04:41.588 --> 00:04:42.000
products.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.000
It can also help you assess cross-marketing opportunities.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:52.000
Each report in the Brand Analytics tool can be filtered using drop-down menus at the top

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:56.000
or customized using specific column selections.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:02.000
For more information about how a specific metric is calculated, review our metrics glossary.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:09.579
You can also download a copy of any Brand Analytics report for your records or to perform additional

00:05:09.579 --> 00:05:10.000
calculations.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.000
This concludes our intro to Brand Analytics.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:19.000
If you'd like step-by-step instructions for using one or more of the reports we've reviewed,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.000
see our series of Brand Analytics modules in Seller University.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:27.000
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon Store!
